-- Q1376: Professional Responsibilities [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Raise the concern and, if unresolved, follow the firm''s conflict resolution","Comply with the partner because the partner has final engagement authority","Immediately report the partner to the AICPA ethics division","Comply with the instruction but document the disagreement in workpapers"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 220, audit team members must exercise professional judgment and not subordinate it improperly. The staff accountant should express the concern to the engagement partner, and if unresolved, follow the firm''s internal conflict resolution procedures for consultation with more senior personnel.
Wrong (B): Complying without question would constitute improper subordination of professional judgment under AU-C 220.
Wrong (C): Immediately reporting to the AICPA bypasses the firm''s internal resolution process, which should be pursued first.
Wrong (D): Documenting disagreement while still complying does not resolve the underlying issue of potentially insufficient evidence.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1376;

-- Q1378: Quality Management [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Maximize firm profitability through efficient resource allocation","Guarantee that all audit opinions issued by the firm are correct","Provide reasonable assurance the firm fulfills its professional responsibilities","Ensure compliance with all client requests regarding audit procedures"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under SQMS No. 1, the objective of a quality management system is to provide reasonable assurance that the firm and its personnel fulfill their responsibilities in accordance with professional standards and applicable legal requirements, and that engagement reports are appropriate.
Wrong (A): Maximizing profitability is a business objective, not the purpose of a quality management system.
Wrong (B): SQMS No. 1 provides reasonable assurance, not absolute guarantees that all opinions are correct.
Wrong (D): Complying with client requests is not the objective; the system ensures compliance with professional standards.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1378;

-- Q1384: Quality Management [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The firm''s designated engagement quality reviewer","The chief executive officer or managing partner of the firm","The AICPA Peer Review Board overseeing the firm","Each individual engagement partner for their engagements"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under SQMS No. 1, ultimate responsibility for the system of quality management rests with the firm''s leadership — specifically the chief executive officer, managing partner, or equivalent. The overall system design, implementation, and operation is a leadership responsibility.
Wrong (A): The engagement quality reviewer evaluates specific engagements but does not bear ultimate system responsibility.
Wrong (C): The AICPA Peer Review Board conducts external reviews but does not manage the firm''s internal quality system.
Wrong (D): Individual engagement partners are responsible for their engagements, not the firm''s overall quality management system.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1384;

-- Q1387: Quality Management [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Establish policies for evaluating client acceptance and continuance decisions","Accept all potential clients to maximize the firm''s total revenue","Accept only clients who are referred by the firm''s existing clients","Continue all existing relationships unless the client requests termination"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SQMS No. 1, the acceptance and continuance component requires the firm to establish policies for evaluating whether to accept or continue client relationships. Key considerations include management integrity, firm competence and resources, ethical compliance, and whether the engagement can be performed per professional standards.
Wrong (B): Accepting all clients without evaluation violates the acceptance and continuance component of SQMS No. 1.
Wrong (C): Limiting acceptance to referrals is a business practice, not a quality management requirement.
Wrong (D): Continuing all relationships without evaluation fails to address risks from changed client circumstances.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1387;

-- Q1388: Quality Management [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Disregard the finding because documentation is secondary to audit quality","Investigate the root cause and implement remedial actions for improvement","Immediately terminate the engagement partners who are responsible","Report the documentation finding to the SEC for regulatory action"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under SQMS No. 1, the firm must investigate root causes of identified deficiencies and implement appropriate remedial actions. For documentation deficiencies, this might include additional training, revised templates, or increased supervisory review to address the root cause.
Wrong (A): Documentation is integral to audit quality; ignoring deficiencies would violate SQMS No. 1 monitoring requirements.
Wrong (C): Immediate termination is disproportionate; remediation should be constructive and address the underlying cause.
Wrong (D): Internal documentation deficiencies are addressed through the firm''s quality management system, not reported to the SEC.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1388;

-- Q1391: Quality Management [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Accept the team''s judgment since the reviewer should not override the partner","Override the engagement team''s conclusion and revise the audit report","Ignore the concern and complete the review to avoid delaying issuance","Discuss the concern with the partner and withhold concurrence if unresolved"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under SQMS No. 2, when the engagement quality reviewer has unresolved concerns about significant judgments, the reviewer should discuss them with the engagement partner. If concerns remain unresolved, the reviewer must not provide concurrence and the report cannot be issued.
Wrong (A): Accepting without question undermines the purpose of the engagement quality review process.
Wrong (B): The reviewer does not have authority to override the team''s conclusions or unilaterally change the report.
Wrong (C): Ignoring concerns to avoid delay would violate the reviewer''s responsibility under SQMS No. 2.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1391;

-- Q1394: Quality Management [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Focus exclusively on profitability targets and firm growth objectives","Delegate all quality management responsibilities to junior-level staff","Foster a quality culture supported by actions, messages, and resources","Establish governance structures identical to those of public companies"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under SQMS No. 1, the governance and leadership component requires firm leadership to establish and promote a culture recognizing quality as essential. Leadership must demonstrate commitment through actions, allocate sufficient resources, and establish accountability for quality at all levels.
Wrong (A): Focusing exclusively on profitability without balancing quality contradicts the governance and leadership requirements.
Wrong (B): Delegating quality responsibilities to junior staff fails to establish the required tone at the top.
Wrong (D): SQMS No. 1 does not require public-company governance structures; it requires quality-focused leadership appropriate to the firm.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1394;

-- Q1395: Quality Management [medium/L4]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The report can be released with the reviewer''s objection noted in a memo","The reviewer must resign from the review to avoid delaying the engagement","The team must address the concern and satisfy the reviewer before release","The matter should be deferred to the firm''s next annual inspection cycle"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under SQMS No. 2, the engagement report cannot be dated or released until the engagement quality review is completed, including resolution of all matters raised by the reviewer. The team must perform additional procedures to address the going concern concern before the reviewer provides concurrence.
Wrong (A): Releasing the report over the reviewer''s objection violates SQMS No. 2''s requirement for completed review.
Wrong (B): The reviewer cannot resign to expedite issuance; the review must be completed with concerns resolved.
Wrong (D): Deferring to annual inspection would delay necessary action and violate the requirement for pre-issuance resolution.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1395;

-- Q1399: Quality Management [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Issue a firm-wide policy reminder without addressing the individual partner","Remove the partner from all engagements and terminate them immediately","Reduce the partner''s compensation without explanation or further action","Provide targeted coaching, enhanced review, and follow-up to verify improvement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under SQMS No. 1, effective remediation addresses both the systemic issue and the individual performance gap. Targeted coaching, enhanced supervisory review, and follow-up monitoring are proportionate and constructive responses to documentation deficiencies.
Wrong (A): A firm-wide reminder alone does not address the individual partner''s persistent documentation failures.
Wrong (B): Immediate removal is disproportionate unless the deficiency reflects incompetence or unwillingness to improve.
Wrong (C): Reducing compensation without explanation or corrective support does not address the root cause of the deficiency.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1399;

-- Q1410: Quality Management [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Risks are assessed first, then responses are designed to address each risk","Each quality risk must have exactly one corresponding response designed","Responses are designed first, then risks are identified to justify them","Quality risks and responses operate independently of each other"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SQMS No. 1, the firm identifies and assesses quality risks and then designs and implements one or more responses to address each assessed risk. The responses must be proportionate to the risk, and a single response may address multiple risks.
Wrong (B): A single risk may require multiple responses; a one-to-one correspondence is not required.
Wrong (C): The process flows from risk identification to response design, not the reverse.
Wrong (D): Risks and responses are directly linked; responses must address the specific risks identified.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1410;

-- Q1425: Government Auditing Standards [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Only the entity''s management for internal corrective action","Only the Government Accountability Office for federal oversight","The general public through an official press release or bulletin","Those charged with governance and, when required, oversight bodies"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GAGAS paragraphs 6.40-6.41, auditors must communicate findings of fraud, noncompliance, and significant deficiencies to those charged with governance and to appropriate officials of the organizations requiring or arranging for the audit. Written reporting ensures oversight bodies can take corrective action.
Wrong (A): Communicating only to management without including those charged with governance does not satisfy GAGAS requirements.
Wrong (B): Findings are not reported solely to the GAO; the primary recipients are those charged with governance and arranging officials.
Wrong (C): GAGAS does not require public disclosure through press releases; findings are communicated through the audit report.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1425;

-- Q1427: Government Auditing Standards [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["$250,000 regardless of total federal awards expended","$500,000 regardless of total federal awards expended","The larger of $750,000 or 3% of total awards, with a ceiling","10% of total federal awards expended by the entity"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under the Uniform Guidance (2 CFR 200.518), a Type A program has expenditures exceeding the larger of $750,000 or a percentage of total federal awards (3% for entities up to $100 million), subject to a ceiling. This threshold determines which programs may be tested as major programs.
Wrong (A): $250,000 is not a recognized threshold for Type A classification under the Uniform Guidance.
Wrong (B): $500,000 is below the $750,000 base amount in the current Uniform Guidance definition.
Wrong (D): 10% of total awards is not the defined threshold; the Uniform Guidance uses 3% (or lower for larger entities) with the $750,000 floor.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1427;

-- Q1431: Government Auditing Standards [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["30 days after receipt, or 9 months after period end, whichever is earlier","60 calendar days after the end of the entity''s fiscal year","90 calendar days after the audit report is completed and issued","120 calendar days after the end of the entity''s fiscal year"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under 2 CFR 200.512, the reporting package including the SF-SAC must be submitted to the Federal Audit Clearinghouse within 30 calendar days after receipt of the auditor''s report, or within 9 months after the end of the audit period, whichever is earlier.
Wrong (B): 60 days after fiscal year-end is not the correct timeframe; the deadline is tied to report receipt, not fiscal year-end.
Wrong (C): 90 days after audit completion is not the standard; the Uniform Guidance specifies 30 days after report receipt.
Wrong (D): 120 days after fiscal year-end exceeds the actual requirement and uses the wrong triggering event.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1431;

-- Q1434: Government Auditing Standards [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The entity must have total federal expenditures below $1 million","The entity must be classified as a state-level government entity","Unmodified opinions and no material weaknesses for the prior two years","The entity must have fewer than 100 employees on its payroll"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under 2 CFR 200.520, low-risk auditee status requires that the entity received unmodified opinions on both the financial statements and compliance for major programs in the two most recent audit periods, with no material weaknesses. Low-risk auditees benefit from reduced audit coverage of 20% versus 40%.
Wrong (A): Federal expenditure amount determines the single audit threshold, not low-risk auditee qualification.
Wrong (B): Low-risk status is available to all types of entities, not limited to state governments.
Wrong (D): Employee count is not a criterion for low-risk auditee status under the Uniform Guidance.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1434;

-- Q1435: Government Auditing Standards [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["An efficiency finding regarding resource utilization","An internal control deficiency in financial oversight","A financial statement misstatement requiring adjustment","A compliance finding for noncompliance with grant provisions"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GAGAS, using federal funds for unauthorized purposes constitutes noncompliance with the terms and conditions of the grant agreement. This compliance finding must be reported in the auditor''s report on compliance and internal control, with questioned costs quantified in the schedule of findings.
Wrong (A): Efficiency findings relate to resource utilization, not unauthorized expenditures that violate grant terms.
Wrong (B): While an internal control deficiency may exist, the primary finding is noncompliance with grant provisions.
Wrong (C): This is a compliance issue with the grant agreement, not merely a financial statement misstatement.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1435;

-- Q1436: Government Auditing Standards [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Only the financial reporting requirements for each major program","All 12 compliance requirement types regardless of program applicability","Only the procurement and suspension or debarment requirements","Applicable requirements that could have a direct and material effect"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Uniform Guidance, the auditor must test compliance requirements applicable to each major program that could have a direct and material effect. The OMB Compliance Supplement identifies up to 12 types, but only those relevant to the specific program are tested.
Wrong (A): Financial reporting is just one of up to 12 compliance requirement types; the auditor tests all applicable types.
Wrong (B): Not all 12 types apply to every program; the auditor determines applicability based on the Compliance Supplement.
Wrong (C): Procurement and suspension/debarment are only two of the potential requirement types that may apply.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1436;

-- Q1439: Government Auditing Standards [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Only the fee amount charged for the nonaudit services provided","Threats identified, safeguards applied, and the independence rationale","A blanket statement asserting that no independence threats exist","Nothing, because nonaudit services do not require documentation"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the Yellow Book, auditors must document their evaluation of threats to independence when performing nonaudit services. The documentation must include specific threats identified, safeguards applied to reduce threats to an acceptable level, and the rationale supporting the conclusion that independence is not impaired.
Wrong (A): Documenting only the fee is insufficient; the Yellow Book requires a full threat-and-safeguard evaluation.
Wrong (C): A blanket statement does not meet the requirement to identify specific threats and document applied safeguards.
Wrong (D): The Yellow Book explicitly requires documentation for nonaudit services provided to audit clients.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1439;
